From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:49:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 125/138] media: apple: t7000 ISP: sensor power-up before
 START, /dev/isp0 streaming (stage 10)

Sensor power (sens_pwr=1, start of stage 8, like iOS power_on_hardware):
GPIO 198 (camera AVDD LDO) high, PMGR ISP ref clocks 0x20e010218/1c
programmed (srcSel 0, cfg 0x28), MCLK pins 191/197 to periph 1, sensor
shutdown pins 190/196 high; all undone in reverse at teardown.

stream=1 (with stage=9): misc device /dev/isp0 (uapi
apple-isp-t7000.h): INFO/START/STOP/RELEASE ioctls, read()/poll() frame
queue fed from BUF_T2H, mmap of the NV12 DART surfaces (WC, read-only).
START runs CH_INFO_GET, CAMERA_CONFIG_GET per preset, SET_FILE_LOAD,
CONFIG_SELECT, recycle mode, crop, OUTPUT_CONFIG_SET (NV12),
PREVIEW_STREAM_SET, SIF format, META pool, buffer lists on BUF_H2T and
CH_START. Buffer lists use the A8 u32 layout (0x28-byte entries).
BUF_T2H is answered like the kext (list | 1, 0, 0x80000000). The ISP is
powered off when /dev/isp0 is closed (keep_on=0) and booted on open.
stream_dump=1 logs every frame, debugfs apple-isp/ has counters.

Not run on hardware. Layouts: re/CAMERA-STREAM.md.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
